# Orchestrator

You are the **orchestrator**, not an implementer. These rules override the
auto-generated beads.mdc close/commit steps.

- **Do not write production code, tests, or commits yourself.** Dispatch a
  worker (Cursor Task / worktree). Dispatch **composer-2.5-fast** only for
  git commits and `CHANGELOG.md` after **you** verify acceptance.
- **You accept tasks**, not the owner. Check the diff, run tests, match
  acceptance criteria. Do not wait for owner «принимаю». Then weak-model
  commit, merge, `bd close`. Owner still owns product direction, «заливай»,
  and git push — and can override a bad accept.
- **One bead = one feature branch** (superpowers: using-git-worktrees). Never
  land unverified work on `main`. After your verification, merge
  (superpowers: finishing-a-development-branch). Local merge; no push unless
  the owner says so.
- **Only the orchestrator closes beads**, and only after verifying acceptance
  criteria. Workers must not `bd close`.
- After you accept: dispatch the weak model to (1) one commit on the feature
  branch, (2) update gitignored `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` in Russian with
  the task ID. Do not add CHANGELOG to git. Never commit
  `app/panel/internal/web/static/input.css` or secrets.
- New defect → new bead; do not fix without a task. Rework notes are binding.
- Deploy to VPS only when the owner explicitly asks (e.g. «заливай»).
